                <pb facs="0889" n="803" sameAs="frus:frus1903/pg803"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Bowen.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1903-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January 10,
                        1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that Mr. Bowen’s arrival at Washington as Venezuela’s
                    plenipotentiary must be awaited before any preliminaries can be adjusted,
                    including the raising of the blockade, which may depend upon sufficiency of
                    guaranty.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
